<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <a href="/manage/insights">Insights</a> compares how busy the venue was (laser games played) with how many
        staff were working, so you can see where the rota could follow demand more closely. Choose the
        <strong>Location</strong> and a date range (<strong>From</strong> and <strong>To</strong>, or a preset number of weeks).
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The figures">
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Games</strong> and <strong>Players</strong> in the range.</li>
            <li><strong>Clocked hours</strong>: time staff were clocked in, breaks included.</li>
            <li><strong>Rota hours</strong>: published shifts, with breaks taken off.</li>
            <li><strong>Labour hours per game</strong>: all clocked time, including setting up, divided by games.</li>
            <li><strong>Games per staff hour</strong>: the other way round. Higher means busier for the staff on.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            Games are counted from the kiosks set to that location, so give every kiosk its location on
            Clients. Hours outside the location's opening hours only count when games were played or staff
            were in, so set the opening hours on Companies &amp; Locations too. Without staff scheduling
            switched on, only the game figures are shown. Use <strong>Export CSV</strong> to
            download the figures for the range.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
